                                     "cache_prompt": false,                                                                                                                               
                                     "type": "text",                                                                                                                                      
                                     "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on                                                                                                    
                             /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources/tscircuit_operation_manual.md:\n     1\t# `tscircuit` Operational                  
                             Guide: Component Creation, Modules & Assembly\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview\n     4\t\n     5\tThis guide provides the necessary instructions               
                             to create custom components from datasheets, organize them into modular groups, and assemble them into a functional circuit. It relies on                    
                             explicit pin mapping, modular grouping with auto-layout, and net-based connectivity.\n     6\t\n     7\t## 1. Creating Custom Components\n                   
                             8\t\n     9\tTo create a new component (e.g., an IC), you must wrap the component definition in a `.tsx` file.\n    10\t\n    11\t### A.                     
                             Importing Footprints\n    12\t\n    13\t`tscircuit` supports direct import of KiCAD (`.kicad_mod`) footprints.\n    14\t\n    15\t  *                        
                             **Source:** Obtain the correct `.kicad_mod` file.\n    16\t  * **Syntax:** `import customFootprint from \"./path/to/footprint.kicad_mod\"`\n                 
                             17\t\n    18\t### B. Defining the Component Symbol (MANDATORY PROPS)\n    19\t\n    20\tUse the `<chip />` primitive.\n    21\t\n    22\t  *                 
                             **Footprint:** Pass the imported variable to the `footprint` prop.\n    23\t  * **Pin Mapping:** Use `pinLabels` to map physical pin numbers to              
                             datasheet names.\n    24\t  * **Mandatory Prop Handling:**\n    25\t      * **Rule:** Your component **MUST** extend `CommonLayoutProps` and                 
                             spread `{...props}` onto the underlying `<chip />`.\n    26\t      * **Reason:** This allows the parent circuit to control positioning (`schX`,              
                             `pcbX`) and rotation.\n    27\t\n    28\t### C. Standard Component Template\n    29\t\n    30\t**File:**                                                     
                             `lib/Components/GenericControllerIC.tsx`\n    31\t\n    32\t```typescript\n    33\timport type { CommonLayoutProps } from \"tscircuit\"\n                    
                             34\timport QFP_Footprint from \"../footprints/QFP32_Generic.kicad_mod\"\n    35\t\n    36\t// 1. MANDATORY: Interface must extend                            
                             CommonLayoutProps\n    37\tinterface Props extends CommonLayoutProps {\n    38\t  name: string\n    39\t}\n    40\t\n    41\texport const                    
                             GenericControllerIC = (props: Props) => {\n    42\t  return (\n    43\t    <chip\n    44\t      footprint={QFP_Footprint}\n    45\t                          
                             pinLabels={{\n    46\t        pin1: \"VDD\",\n    47\t        pin2: \"GND\",\n    48\t        // ... mappings\n    49\t        pin32: \"VSS\"\n              
                             50\t      }}\n    51\t      // 2. CRITICAL: Spread props to enable positioning\n    52\t      {...props}\n    53\t    />\n    54\t   )\n                     
                             55\t}\n    56\t```\n    57\t\n    58\t-----\n    59\t\n    60\t## 2. Modular Circuit Design with `<group />`\n    61\t\n    62\tThe `<group />`              
                             element is a container used to organize multiple components into a single block. It is highly recommended to use `<group>` with **Flex** or                  
                             **Grid** props to handle layout automatically, rather than calculating manual coordinates for every sub-component.\n    63\t\n    64\t### A.                 
                             Creating a Reusable Module\n    65\t\n    66\tWrap related components and traces inside a `<group />`.\n    67\t\n    68\t  * **Mandatory Prop               
                             Handling:** Your Module **MUST** accept `CommonLayoutProps` and spread them onto the root `<group>` tag.\n    69\t\n    70\t**File:**                        
                             `lib/Modules/PowerInput.tsx`\n    71\t\n    72\t```typescript\n    73\timport type { CommonLayoutProps } from \"tscircuit\"\n    74\t\n                      
                             75\tinterface Props extends CommonLayoutProps {\n    76\t  namePrefix?: string \n    77\t}\n    78\t\n    79\texport const PowerInputModule =                
                             (props: Props) => {\n    80\t  return (\n    81\t    // CRITICAL: Spread props here to allow moving the whole group\n    82\t    <group                      
                             {...props}>\n    83\t      {/* Passives must have a footprint and name */}\n    84\t      <resistor name=\"R_Fuse\" resistance=\"10\"                        
                             footprint=\"0603\" schX={0} schY={0} />\n    85\t      <capacitor name=\"C_Bulk\" capacitance=\"100uF\" footprint=\"1206\" schX={10} schY={0}                
